Interpreter paths that cost calls on 32-bit PowerPC.

An int32 add, subtract or multiply that overflows made its double from
the 64-bit result, which on 32-bit PowerPC is a call to libgcc's
__floatdidf. The result is now made from the two int32 operands in
double arithmetic: the same value (an add or subtract of two int32 is
exact in a double; a product is rounded once either way), with the
processor's floating-point unit. Cloudflare's Turnstile overflows int32
in its hashing all the time: __floatdidf was 0.5% of its time in the
guest.

The interpreter is too large for GCC to inline JS_FreeValue into it,
so each value it dropped was a call (99 call sites). It now decrements
the reference count in line and calls only to free.

--- a/quickjs.c
+++ b/quickjs.c
@@ -18428,6 +18428,19 @@
     return can_store_error_stack(exc) || can_add_backtrace(exc);
 }
 
+/* The interpreter drops a reference in line: a call per value freed cost
+   more than the decrement on 32-bit PowerPC, where the interpreter is too
+   large for GCC to inline JS_FreeValue into it. */
+static inline __attribute__((always_inline))
+void js_free_value_inline(JSContext *ctx, JSValue v)
+{
+    if (JS_VALUE_HAS_REF_COUNT(v)) {
+        if (--JS_REF_COUNT(JS_VALUE_GET_PTR(v)) <= 0)
+            js_free_value_rt(ctx->rt, v);
+    }
+}
+#define JS_FreeValue(ctx, v) js_free_value_inline(ctx, v)
+
 /* argv[] is modified if (flags & JS_CALL_FLAG_COPY_ARGV) = 0. */
 static JSValue JS_CallInternal(JSContext *caller_ctx, JSValueConst func_obj,
                                JSValueConst this_obj, JSValueConst new_target,
@@ -20510,7 +20523,8 @@
